research/audit/wave12-certifier-tasks/a6-cex-mean-value-equality-fails-for-a-vector-valued-function.md-383-[L5] Canonical naturals are positive and strictly increasing, and carry sums to sums and products to products, so $\iota(2)^{2} = \iota(4)$, $\iota(3)^{2} = \iota(9)$, $\iota(4)+\iota(9) = \iota(13)$ and $\iota(3) \ne \iota(4)$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]], [[def-canonical-natural]]).
